  <div class="print-section">
    <h2>TLDR</h2>
    <p>Doing Thanksgiving across two days. Turkey's marinating in koji (Japanese fermented rice) for deep flavor and tenderness. Thursday: making stock, baking rolls, homemade cranberry orange compote, and eggnog basque cheesecake, having a light Japanese-fusion dinner. Friday: the full feast—koji turkey, homemade cranberry compote, dressed maple sage butter brussels sprouts with sausage, hasselback potatoes, stuffing, gravy, pumpkin pie, and that cheesecake. Saturday and beyond: leftovers pie—everything layered into one reheatable dish with potatoes on top, stuffing on bottom, and gravy holding it all together.</p>
